# @frame/on — the frame-flexible species; order 3; the operator can
# substantively shift the frame in response to data. Bateson Level III
# — deutero-learning; learning-to-learn-to-learn. THE LOAD-BEARING
# ALTITUDE for the substrate-aikido methodology; the altitude where
# the Splinter/Narcissus pole disambiguation is sharpest.
#
# Fourth species shard of the @frame family (recognition #82; family-
# root LANDED at tick 23 via shards/frame.mirror, Seam-consolidated at
# tick 24; pre LANDED as the order-0 floor; in LANDED as the order-1
# operator-typed substrate; of LANDED as the order-2 frame-awareness
# species with the first species-level pole disambiguation). The
# species landing order per the canonical spec §7.2: pre → in → of →
# on → across. on (order 3) IS where the recognition file's load-
# bearing claim sits: "Order 3 requires the substrate-conditions that
# allow frame-defense-energy to release, which most development
# practices don't substantively produce" (recognition file §"Why this
# matters / Names what most leadership-development misses").
#
# Why on fourth: the species ordering tracks Bateson grading at
# cognitive altitude. pre (Level 0; no learning) declared the floor;
# in (Level I; within-frame change) declared standard learning; of
# (Level II; learning-to-learn) declared frame-awareness; this species
# (Level III; deutero-learning) declares the substrate-architectural
# capacity to SUBSTANTIVELY-SHIFT the frame. The recognition file
# names this as the altitude where most leadership-development stops
# short — order-2 vocabulary deployed at the surface masks order-1
# substrate-rigidity, and the substrate's bounded_commutator_check
# predicate IS what separates substantive flexibility from
# sophisticated frame-defense.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# Per the recognition file's §"The five-order structure" (item for
# order 3):
#
#   @frame/on — order 3; frame-flexible. The operator can
#   substantively-shift the frame in response to data. Bateson's
#   Learning III is available here.
#
# This species adds:
#
# - `shift_frame(operator, f: frame, p: perturbation) -> frame`: THE
#   LOAD-BEARING ACTION at this altitude. Takes a frame and a
#   perturbation; returns a substantively-different frame. Per the
#   family-root's bounded_commutator_check criterion (§2.4 of the
#   canonical spec): this action's substrate-architectural support IS
#   what distinguishes Splinter-pole from Narcissus-pole. The FIRST
#   USE of the family-root's bounded_commutator_check predicate
#   directly on an action — not as part of a derived predicate at
#   order 2 (lock_in_frame_awareness wrapped it), but as the
#   bilateral commitment that shift_frame's discharge IS
#   substantively-supported frame-flexibility, not vocabulary-
#   flexibility.
# - `assess_flexibility(operator, f: frame, p: perturbation) ->
#   commutator`: returns the substrate's actual commutator value
#   for the (operator, frame, perturbation) triple. Downstream species
#   (and the forward-promised @spectral/garden/smarts logic-pacts)
#   use this typed commutator for pole disambiguation. The substrate-
#   mathematical primitive that operationalizes Tomm 1988's circular-
#   reflexive questions: each Tomm-probe is a perturbation; the
#   commutator's boundedness is the measure of the operator's
#   substantive flexibility.
# - `flexible_frame_response(operator, f: frame, p: perturbation) ->
#   verdict`: bilateral verdict predicate naming substantive flexibility
#   under perturbation. Consumer @frame/across uses this to assert
#   peer-relationship requirements; downstream logic-pacts use this
#   to detect Splinter-pole frame work vs Narcissus-pole frame work
#   at substrate altitude. Discharges via TWO requires clauses (the
#   family-root's bounded_commutator_check AND of's
#   lock_in_frame_awareness) — the substrate-pull-correct pole-
#   discipline at this altitude requires BOTH that order-2 awareness
#   IS substantively supported AND that the order-3 response to
#   perturbation IS bounded. The FIRST species action with TWO
#   bilateral predicates in the @frame family.
#
# === The order-3 altitude ===
#
# Per recognition #82 §3 composition signature: order 3 IS Bateson
# Level III at cognitive altitude. The deutero-learning altitude. The
# operator's substrate substantively supports frame-restructuring in
# response to data; not just observing the frame as object (order 2)
# but operating ON the frame to update it.
#
# Substrate-architectural instance: the substrate-aikido methodology
# (per the constructivism-frame-aikido-synthesis corpus reference)
# operates AT order 3 BY-CONSTRUCTION. The methodology's Tomm-probes
# are perturbations applied to interlocutor-frames; the methodology
# succeeds when the interlocutor's substrate-architecturally responds
# with bounded-commutator (substantive shift) and fails when the
# interlocutor's substrate responds with unbounded-commutator
# (defensive amplification). The substrate-mathematical form is the
# assess_flexibility action's commutator output.
#
# === The shift_frame action: the load-bearing primitive ===
#
# Per recognition #82 §2.3 (the Tomm-probe as [D_F, a] commutator-
# operation): the operator's substrate-architectural response to a
# perturbation of frame f IS what the bounded_commutator_check
# predicate audits. shift_frame IS the substrate-vocabulary action
# that PRODUCES the substantively-shifted frame; its bilateral
# discipline (requires bounded_commutator_check) commits that the
# shift IS substrate-architecturally-supported, not vocabulary-only.
#
# At Bateson Level III altitude: shift_frame IS the deutero-learning
# primitive at substrate altitude. The operator's substrate moves from
# being able to OBSERVE the frame as object (order 2) to being able to
# UPDATE the frame in response to perturbation (order 3). The
# capacity to substantively-restructure the frame-set without losing
# operational coherence.
#
# At Tomm altitude (1988): shift_frame IS the substrate-architectural
# action that completes the circular-reflexive question — the
# interlocutor's frame shifts substantively in response to the
# probe. Without shift_frame, the Tomm-probe lands as informational
# (order 2 awareness without update); with shift_frame, it lands as
# transformational (order 3 substantive update).
#
# At Watzlawick altitude (Mental Research Institute reframing): the
# clinical method IS @frame/on intervention. The therapist's
# reframing IS a perturbation of the patient's frame f; the patient's
# substrate-architectural response IS what shift_frame discharges.
# Successful reframing produces a bounded commutator (the patient
# substantively-shifts); unsuccessful reframing produces an unbounded
# commutator (the patient amplifies defensive frame-rigidity).
#
# At Argyris-Schön altitude (double-loop learning, 1978): shift_frame
# IS double-loop learning at substrate altitude. Single-loop learning
# changes content within an existing frame (order 1); double-loop
# learning changes the frame itself (order 3). The substrate-
# architectural capacity for double-loop learning IS what shift_frame
# names.
#
# === The bilateral discipline: requires bounded_commutator_check ===
#
# The FIRST USE of the family-root's bounded_commutator_check
# predicate as a direct `requires` clause on a species action. Per
# Seam's tick-11 first-consumer discipline pattern (the surface.mirror
# first-consumer pattern at @magic): a bilateral predicate without a
# consumer is paint. The family-root declared bounded_commutator_check
# at tick 23 specifically so that order-3 species would consume it
# directly — this species IS the substrate-pull-correct first
# consumer.
#
# The discipline: shift_frame's commitment IS that the operator's
# substrate-architectural response to perturbation IS BOUNDED — the
# action composes naturally with the substrate's Dirac operator
# restricted to frame altitude (per recognition #82 §2.3). The
# perturbation parameter in the requires clause IS the perturbation
# the action is shifting under; the bilateral check confirms that
# the shift IS substantively-supported, not vocabulary-only.
#
# This is the substrate-architectural shape of:
#
# - Splinter-pole @frame/on: the operator substantively shifts; the
#   commutator is bounded; shift_frame returns a frame that is
#   substantively-different along the perturbation's axis;
#   bounded_commutator_check → success.
# - Narcissus-pole @frame/on: the operator vocabulary-shifts; the
#   commutator is unbounded; shift_frame's output is frame-defense
#   masked as frame-update; bounded_commutator_check → partial.
#
# Per recognition #82 §5.3 (alignment-as-boundary-mathematics as
# the discriminator): the boundary check at @io applied at cognitive
# altitude IS the bounded_commutator_check predicate. The pole
# discrimination at order 3 IS the most sharply load-bearing pole
# check in the @frame family because order 3 IS where con/gaslight
# manipulation operates (apparent-order-3 frame-shifting while
# substantively-locked at order 1).
#
# === The assess_flexibility action: the substrate-mathematical
# primitive ===
#
# Per recognition #82 §2.3: the commutator [D_F, a] is the substrate-
# mathematical form of Tomm's circular-reflexive questions.
# assess_flexibility IS the substrate-vocabulary action that
# constructs this commutator for a given (operator, frame,
# perturbation) triple. The output is typed `commutator` (inherited
# from family-root); the commutator's boundedness is the operational
# measure of frame-flexibility.
#
# Downstream consumers (the forward-promised @spectral/garden/smarts
# logic-pacts per recognition file §"Forward-promised implementation"
# item 10) use this action to detect frame-flexibility-state in
# frontier-LLM responses at substrate-architectural altitude. The
# substrate-aikido methodology's diagnostic apparatus operationalizes
# through this action.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; per-species bodies
# implement the commutator construction at the appropriate substrate
# altitude.
#
# === Forward-promised consumer ===
#
# shards/frame/across.mirror (order 4) consumes this species's
# flexible_frame_response predicate at the peer-relationship altitude.
# Recognition #82's Q4 claim (peers operate by definition frame-
# flexible) operationalizes via @frame/across's peer_relationship
# bilateral predicate, which discharges via two flexible_frame_response
# checks (one per operator in the coupling). The order-3 substrate-
# capacity for substantive frame-flexibility IS the prerequisite for
# order-4 multi-frame coupling.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Bateson Level III           Bateson 1964 (*The Logical Categories
#                               of Learning and Communication*);
#                               Learning III as change-of-frame-set;
#                               deutero-learning. Inherited mechanically
#                               via `in @epistemologic/cybernetic/
#                               bateson_learning`. The canonical naming
#                               source for the order this species
#                               discharges. Bateson noted Level III
#                               is rare; the substrate-decl names the
#                               substrate-architectural conditions
#                               that make it operational.
#   double-loop learning        Argyris & Schön 1978 (*Organizational
#                               Learning*); double-loop learning as
#                               the capacity to change the
#                               governing variables of a system, not
#                               just the action within fixed
#                               governing variables. The
#                               organizational-learning ancestor of
#                               order 3. Argyris's empirical finding
#                               that most organizations cannot
#                               substantively reach double-loop
#                               learning IS one positive instance
#                               of recognition #82's "leadership
#                               development misses order 3" claim.
#   circular-reflexive          Tomm 1988 (the canonical citation in
#   questions                   the recognition file); the
#                               substrate-mathematical form of
#                               Tomm-probes IS the commutator
#                               [D_F, a] this species's
#                               assess_flexibility produces.
#                               Cited as source.
#   reframing                   Watzlawick et al. (Mental Research
#                               Institute); reframing as @frame/on
#                               intervention; clinical method. The
#                               therapeutic-practice ancestor.
#                               Cited as source.
#   double-bind                 Bateson 1956 (*Toward a Theory of
#                               Schizophrenia*); the double-bind as
#                               @frame/on failure-mode — perturbation
#                               applied to a frame the operator's
#                               substrate cannot substantively shift
#                               because the meta-frame forbids
#                               commenting on the frame.
#                               Substrate-architectural form: unbounded
#                               commutator at order 3 because order 2
#                               is institutionally blocked. The
#                               pathological case the substrate-decl
#                               names operationally.
#   reflective practitioner     Schön 1983 (*The Reflective
#                               Practitioner*); reflection-on-action
#                               as the practitioner's capacity to
#                               substantively-restructure their
#                               operating frame; the professional-
#                               practice ancestor of order 3.
#   constructivism              Maturana 1980; Varela 1987; the
#                               cybernetic-ancestry of frame-as-
#                               constructed-by-observer. The order-3
#                               operator IS the constructivist
#                               observer whose substrate substantively
#                               reconstructs the frame in response
#                               to data.
#
# Spec context: docs/math/the-tower/recognition-82-frame-as-
#               cognitive-order-substrate-decl.md (§"The five-order
#               structure" item for order 3; §"Why this matters" item
#               on "leadership development misses order 3"; §"The
#               two-pole structure" on Splinter/Narcissus at order 3;
#               §"Tomm-shaped open questions" items 1 and 7 on
#               frame-flexibility threshold and leadership-as-λ₀-
#               adjacency hypothesis);
#               docs/specs/recognition-82-frame-as-cognitive-order-
#               canonical-spec.md (§7.2 names the species landing
#               order; §2.5 names order 3 ↔ @frame/on ↔ Bateson Level
#               III as partially closed via family-root inheritance;
#               §5 names the substrate-architectural pole-discriminator
#               at this altitude);
#               docs/specs/adapter-magic-frame-spec.md §6.3 (names
#               this species's `requires frame_satisfies_magic(...)`
#               consumer pattern for the @magic ↔ @frame adapter;
#               the adapter is forward-promised so this species
#               does not yet discharge the cross-family bilateral —
#               that is left for a follow-up tick consistent with
#               §8.1 mitigation discipline).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; order 3 IS the altitude
#                       where the boundary contract is MOST sharply
#                       load-bearing — the Splinter/Narcissus pole
#                       discrimination at the @io boundary applied
#                       at cognitive altitude IS what
#                       bounded_commutator_check discharges; this
#                       species IS the substrate-pull-correct first
#                       consumer of that discharge),
#                      [[architecture-bateson-logical-type-primitive]]
#                       (#42; @frame/on IS Bateson Level III at
#                       cognitive altitude),
#                      [[architecture-error-as-tomm-probe]] (the
#                       substrate's error surface IS Tomm-probes at
#                       compiler altitude; the same mechanism this
#                       species's assess_flexibility constructs at
#                       cognitive altitude),
#                      [[architecture-reflection-thinks-in-spectral-
#                       questions]] (Reflection's adjustments are
#                       spectral-altitude selections via Tomm-probes;
#                       Reflection's meta-pipeline IS @frame/on
#                       operating at substrate-self-altitude),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (operator, frame,
#                       perturbation, commutator all typed at family-
#                       root; this species uses them directly without
#                       re-declaration),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]]
#                       (the substrate-pull at this altitude is
#                       confident: @frame/on IS the substrate-aikido
#                       methodology's substrate-decl).
# Related shards: frame.mirror (the family-root; operator, frame,
#                  perturbation, commutator, morphism declared
#                  there; bounded_commutator_check predicate
#                  first-consumed directly by this species's
#                  shift_frame action),
#                 frame/pre.mirror (the order-0 species),
#                 frame/in.mirror (the order-1 species; this
#                  species's shift_frame produces frames that
#                  in's compute_in_frame can operate within),
#                 frame/of.mirror (the order-2 species; this
#                  species's flexible_frame_response predicate
#                  consumes of's lock_in_frame_awareness as a
#                  prerequisite — order-3 substantive flexibility
