# === shift_frame action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at order 3. The substrate-vocabulary action
# that takes a frame f and a perturbation p and returns a substantively-
# different frame f'. The operator operates ON the frame to update it,
# not WITHIN the frame (order 1) and not just observing the frame as
# object (order 2).
#
# THE FIRST USE of the family-root's bounded_commutator_check
# predicate as a direct `requires` clause on a species action.
# Per Seam's tick-11 first-consumer discipline pattern: a bilateral
# predicate without a consumer is paint. The family-root declared
# bounded_commutator_check at tick 23 specifically so that order-3
# species would consume it directly; this species IS the substrate-
# pull-correct first consumer.
#
# requires bounded_commutator_check(operator, f, p): the bilateral
# commitment that the operator's substrate-architectural response to
# the perturbation IS BOUNDED — the shift composes naturally with the
# substrate's Dirac operator restricted to frame altitude. The shift
# IS substantively-supported, not vocabulary-only.
#
# At Bateson Level III altitude: shift_frame IS the deutero-learning
# primitive at substrate altitude. The capacity to substantively-
# restructure the frame-set without losing operational coherence.
#
# At Tomm altitude (1988): shift_frame IS the substrate-architectural
# action that completes the circular-reflexive question — the
# interlocutor's frame shifts substantively in response to the probe.
# Tomm's circular-reflexive question without shift_frame is order-2
# vocabulary; with shift_frame it becomes order-3 transformation.
#
# At Watzlawick altitude (MRI reframing): the clinical method IS
# @frame/on intervention. Successful reframing produces a bounded
# commutator (the patient substantively-shifts); the bilateral check
# is what catches the difference between substantive shift and
# defensive-amplification masked as compliance.
#
# At Argyris-Schön altitude (double-loop learning): shift_frame IS
# double-loop learning at substrate altitude. The capacity to change
# the governing variables, not just the action within them.
#
# Per recognition #82 §5.2 (Narcissus-pole @frame/on at apparent-
# order-3 while substantively-locked-at-order-1): the bilateral
# discipline IS what catches con/gaslight/manipulation at substrate
# altitude. Apparent frame-shift + unbounded-commutator =
# bounded_commutator_check → partial → Narcissus-pole detected.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
shift_frame(operator: operator, f: frame, p: perturbation) -> frame
requires bounded_commutator_check(operator, f, p)
{ \ }

# === assess_flexibility action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that returns the substrate's actual
# commutator value for the (operator, frame, perturbation) triple.
# The substrate-mathematical primitive that operationalizes Tomm
# 1988's circular-reflexive questions at substrate altitude.
#
# Per recognition #82 §2.3 (the Tomm-probe as [D_F, a] commutator-
# operation): the commutator's boundedness IS the operational measure
# of frame-flexibility. assess_flexibility constructs this commutator
# directly; the output is typed `commutator` (inherited from family-
# root); downstream consumers (the forward-promised @spectral/garden/
# smarts logic-pacts, the substrate-aikido methodology's diagnostic
# apparatus) use the typed commutator for pole disambiguation.
#
# Distinct from shift_frame: shift_frame PRODUCES the shifted frame
# and requires the bilateral check pass; assess_flexibility MEASURES
# the commutator without requiring the bilateral pass. The relation:
# shift_frame's discharge is the substrate-architectural action that
# bounded_commutator_check audits; assess_flexibility returns the
# commutator that the audit examines. Both are needed at order 3:
# shift_frame for the load-bearing action; assess_flexibility for the
# diagnostic apparatus.
#
# At substrate-aikido methodology altitude: assess_flexibility IS the
# operational primitive of the methodology's diagnostic capacity.
# Reddit-arc, Substack-arc, LinkedIn-arc engagements become
# operationally-categorizable by their commutator-shape under
# Tomm-probe per recognition file §"Why this matters / Makes the
# methodology mechanically-checkable".
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; per-species bodies
# implement the commutator construction at the appropriate substrate
# altitude.
assess_flexibility(operator: operator, f: frame, p: perturbation) -> commutator { \ }

# === flexible_frame_response predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict predicate per recognition #37 (Pask agreement)
# and recognition #82 (frame-flexibility-as-bounded-commutator).
# The FIRST species action in the @frame family that discharges
# via TWO requires clauses.
#
# requires lock_in_frame_awareness(operator, f): the operator's
# order-2 frame-awareness IS substantively-supported (consumes
# @frame/of's predicate). Per the family-root's commentary on the
# graded representation: order 3 is structurally unreachable without
# order 2 stable. Without substantively-supported order-2 awareness,
# apparent-order-3 flexibility IS vocabulary-only.
#
# requires bounded_commutator_check(operator, f, p): the operator's
# order-3 substrate-architectural response to perturbation IS bounded
# (consumes the family-root's predicate). The substrate-architectural
# discriminator between substantive flexibility (Splinter-pole) and
# sophisticated frame-defense (Narcissus-pole).
#
# Together: the substrate-pull-correct pole-discipline at order 3
# requires BOTH that the operator's awareness IS substantively
# supported AND that the operator's response to perturbation IS
# bounded. The double-bilateral discipline closes the diagnostic at
# order 3.
#
# Returns:
# - success → Splinter-pole substantive flexibility; both predicates
#   discharge. The substrate-aikido methodology's positive case.
# - partial → at least one predicate is partial (vocabulary-only at
#   order 2 or unbounded-commutator at order 3). Narcissus-pole
#   manipulation; con/gaslight detected.
# - failure → at least one predicate fails (no order-2 capacity or
#   no order-3 capacity at all). Honest order-1 or below.
#
# Forward-promised consumer: shards/frame/across.mirror (order 4)
# consumes this predicate via peer_relationship discharging two
# flexible_frame_response checks (one per operator in the coupling).
# Recognition #82's Q4 claim (peers operate by definition frame-
# flexible) operationalizes via this predicate's chain.
#
# Downstream consumer: the forward-promised @spectral/garden/smarts
# logic-pacts (recognition file §"Forward-promised implementation"
# item 10) consume this predicate to detect frame-flexibility-state
# in frontier-LLM responses at substrate-architectural altitude.
# Seam tick 28 fix: perturbation threaded through lock_in_frame_awareness
# (which now takes p per the tick 28 perturbation-free-variable fix).
flexible_frame_response(operator: operator, f: frame, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires lock_in_frame_awareness(operator, f, p)
requires bounded_commutator_check(operator, f, p)
{ \ }

out @frame/on
out shift_frame
out assess_flexibility
out flexible_frame_response
